# Service Contracts & Repository Pattern — Study Notes

## Table of Contents
1. [Service Contracts Overview](#1-service-contracts-overview)
2. [The Api/ Folder Structure](#2-the-api-folder-structure)
3. [DataInterface — Pure DTOs](#3-datainterface--pure-dtos)
4. [RepositoryInterface — CRUD + getList](#4-repositoryinterface--crud--getlist)
5. [The @api Annotation](#5-the-api-annotation)
6. [SearchCriteriaInterface Deep Dive](#6-searchcriteriainterface-deep-dive)
7. [Repository Implementation](#7-repository-implementation)
8. [Extension Attributes](#8-extension-attributes)
9. [Critical Gotchas](#9-critical-gotchas)
10. [Hands-On: SearchCriteriaBuilder in Practice](#10-hands-on-searchcriteriabuilder-in-practice)
11. [Quick-Reference Checklist](#quick-reference-checklist)

---

## 1. Service Contracts Overview

A **service contract** is Magento's formal, versioned API layer that sits between consumers (controllers, REST, GraphQL, other modules) and the underlying storage/business logic.

```
+---------------------+
|   API Consumer      |  (Controller, REST endpoint, CLI command)
+---------------------+
          |
          v  calls
+---------------------+
|  RepositoryInterface|  <-- Service Contract (Api/ folder)
+---------------------+
          |
          v  uses
+---------------------+
|  Repository Impl.   |  (Model/ResourceModel layer)
+---------------------+
          |
          v
+---------------------+
|   Database / Cache  |
+---------------------+
```

**Why service contracts exist:**
- Provide a **stable public API** — third-party code calls the interface, not the concrete class
- Enable **substitutability** — the implementation can change without breaking consumers
- Power Magento's **Web API** (REST/SOAP) auto-routing via `webapi.xml`
- Support **plugin interception** at a clean, well-defined boundary

> **Exam focus:** Service contracts decouple consumers from implementations. REST/SOAP endpoints defined in `webapi.xml` map directly to service contract interfaces.

---

## 2. The Api/ Folder Structure

Every module that exposes a service contract follows this directory convention:

```
Vendor/Module/
+-- Api/
|   +-- Data/
|   |   +-- WidgetInterface.php          <-- DTO (DataInterface)
|   |   +-- WidgetSearchResultsInterface.php
|   +-- WidgetRepositoryInterface.php    <-- Repository contract
+-- Model/
|   +-- Widget.php                       <-- Concrete model (implements WidgetInterface)
|   +-- WidgetRepository.php             <-- Concrete repository (implements WidgetRepositoryInterface)
|   +-- ResourceModel/
|       +-- Widget.php
|       +-- Widget/
|           +-- Collection.php
+-- etc/
    +-- di.xml                           <-- preference mappings
```

### di.xml Preference Mapping

```xml
<!-- Vendor/Module/etc/di.xml -->
<config xmlns:xsi="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema-instance"
        xsi:noNamespaceSchemaLocation="urn:magento:framework:ObjectManager/etc/config.xsd">

    <!-- Map interface -> concrete implementation -->
    <preference for="Vendor\Module\Api\WidgetRepositoryInterface"
                type="Vendor\Module\Model\WidgetRepository"/>

    <preference for="Vendor\Module\Api\Data\WidgetInterface"
                type="Vendor\Module\Model\Widget"/>

    <preference for="Vendor\Module\Api\Data\WidgetSearchResultsInterface"
                type="Magento\Framework\Api\SearchResults"/>
</config>
```

> **Exam focus:** The `Api/Data/` subfolder holds **DTOs only**. The `Api/` root holds **repository and service interfaces**. The concrete classes live in `Model/`.

---

## 3. DataInterface — Pure DTOs

A **DataInterface** (DTO — Data Transfer Object) carries data between layers. It has:
- **Getters and setters only**
- **No business logic** — no calculations, no DB calls, no event dispatching
- **No dependencies** on resource models or collections

### Example DataInterface

```php
<?php
// Vendor/Module/Api/Data/WidgetInterface.php

namespace Vendor\Module\Api\Data;

/**
 * @api
 */
interface WidgetInterface
{
    // Field name constants — used in filters, sorting, and DB columns
    const WIDGET_ID   = 'widget_id';
    const NAME        = 'name';
    const SKU         = 'sku';
    const PRICE       = 'price';
    const IS_ACTIVE   = 'is_active';
    const CREATED_AT  = 'created_at';

    /**
     * @return int|null
     */
    public function getId();

    /**
     * @param int $id
     * @return $this
     */
    public function setId($id);

    /**
     * @return string
     */
    public function getName(): string;

    /**
     * @param string $name
     * @return $this
     */
    public function setName(string $name): self;

    /**
     * @return float
     */
    public function getPrice(): float;

    /**
     * @param float $price
     * @return $this
     */
    public function setPrice(float $price): self;

    /**
     * @return \Vendor\Module\Api\Data\WidgetExtensionInterface|null
     */
    public function getExtensionAttributes(): ?WidgetExtensionInterface;

    /**
     * @param \Vendor\Module\Api\Data\WidgetExtensionInterface $extensionAttributes
     * @return $this
     */
    public function setExtensionAttributes(WidgetExtensionInterface $extensionAttributes): self;
}
```

### Concrete Model Implementation

```php
<?php
// Vendor/Module/Model/Widget.php

namespace Vendor\Module\Model;

use Magento\Framework\Model\AbstractModel;
use Vendor\Module\Api\Data\WidgetInterface;

class Widget extends AbstractModel implements WidgetInterface
{
    protected function _construct(): void
    {
        $this->_init(\Vendor\Module\Model\ResourceModel\Widget::class);
    }

    public function getName(): string
    {
        return (string) $this->getData(self::NAME);
    }

    public function setName(string $name): self
    {
        return $this->setData(self::NAME, $name);
    }

    public function getPrice(): float
    {
        return (float) $this->getData(self::PRICE);
    }

    public function setPrice(float $price): self
    {
        return $this->setData(self::PRICE, $price);
    }

    // Extension attributes — generated code handles the actual storage
    public function getExtensionAttributes(): ?\Vendor\Module\Api\Data\WidgetExtensionInterface
    {
        return $this->_getExtensionAttributes();
    }

    public function setExtensionAttributes(
        \Vendor\Module\Api\Data\WidgetExtensionInterface $extensionAttributes
    ): self {
        return $this->_setExtensionAttributes($extensionAttributes);
    }
}
```

> **Exam focus:** DataInterface = **getters + setters only**. Zero business logic. Constants define field names. Must declare `getExtensionAttributes()` / `setExtensionAttributes()` to support extension attributes.

---

## 4. RepositoryInterface — CRUD + getList

The **RepositoryInterface** defines the full CRUD surface plus a search method.

### Standard Method Signatures

```php
<?php
// Vendor/Module/Api/WidgetRepositoryInterface.php

namespace Vendor\Module\Api;

use Magento\Framework\Api\SearchCriteriaInterface;
use Vendor\Module\Api\Data\WidgetInterface;
use Vendor\Module\Api\Data\WidgetSearchResultsInterface;

/**
 * @api
 */
interface WidgetRepositoryInterface
{
    /**
     * Save a widget (create or update).
     *
     * @param \Vendor\Module\Api\Data\WidgetInterface $widget
     * @return \Vendor\Module\Api\Data\WidgetInterface
     * @throws \Magento\Framework\Exception\CouldNotSaveException
     */
    public function save(WidgetInterface $widget): WidgetInterface;

    /**
     * Retrieve widget by ID.
     *
     * @param int $widgetId
     * @return \Vendor\Module\Api\Data\WidgetInterface
     * @throws \Magento\Framework\Exception\NoSuchEntityException
     */
    public function getById(int $widgetId): WidgetInterface;

    /**
     * Retrieve widgets matching search criteria.
     *
     * @param \Magento\Framework\Api\SearchCriteriaInterface $searchCriteria
     * @return \Vendor\Module\Api\Data\WidgetSearchResultsInterface
     */
    public function getList(SearchCriteriaInterface $searchCriteria): WidgetSearchResultsInterface;

    /**
     * Delete widget.
     *
     * @param \Vendor\Module\Api\Data\WidgetInterface $widget
     * @return bool
     * @throws \Magento\Framework\Exception\CouldNotDeleteException
     */
    public function delete(WidgetInterface $widget): bool;

    /**
     * Delete widget by ID.
     *
     * @param int $widgetId
     * @return bool
     * @throws \Magento\Framework\Exception\NoSuchEntityException
     * @throws \Magento\Framework\Exception\CouldNotDeleteException
     */
    public function deleteById(int $widgetId): bool;
}
```

### Exception Contract — Critical Rules

| Scenario | Exception | Never Do |
|---|---|---|
| Entity not found by ID | `NoSuchEntityException` | Return `null` |
| Save fails (DB error) | `CouldNotSaveException` | Return `false` |
| Delete fails | `CouldNotDeleteException` | Silently swallow |
| Invalid search criteria | `InputException` | Return empty array |

> **Exam focus:** `getById()` **MUST throw `NoSuchEntityException`** when the entity doesn't exist. It **NEVER returns `null`**. This is one of the most-tested repository rules.
>
> **Note:** The real `ProductRepositoryInterface` deviates from this generic pattern: `save()` throws `InputException`/`StateException`/`CouldNotSaveException`, `delete()` throws `StateException` (not `CouldNotDeleteException`), and `deleteById($sku)` takes a **SKU string** not an int ID. It also has a `get($sku)` method (by SKU). The pattern above is the **recommended modern convention** for custom repositories.

---

## 5. The @api Annotation

The `@api` PHPDoc annotation is Magento's signal that an interface (or class) is part of the **stable public API surface**.

```php
/**
 * Widget repository interface.
 *
 * @api                          <-- This annotation is the contract marker
 * @since 1.0.0
 */
interface WidgetRepositoryInterface
{
    // ...
}
```

### What @api Means

| Aspect | Detail |
|---|---|
| **Backward compatibility** | Marked code must not have breaking changes in patch/minor releases |
| **Third-party safety** | Extensions can safely depend on `@api`-marked interfaces |
| **Versioning** | Breaking changes require a major version bump |
| **Scope** | Applies to interfaces in `Api/` and `Api/Data/` folders |

### What @api Does NOT Mean

- It does **not** make the class auto-routable via REST (that's `webapi.xml`)
- It does **not** generate any code at compile time
- It is a **convention/documentation signal**, not a PHP language feature

> **Exam focus:** `@api` marks the **stable public API surface**. All interfaces in `Api/` and `Api/Data/` should carry this annotation. It signals backward-compatibility commitment.

---

## 6. SearchCriteriaInterface Deep Dive

`SearchCriteriaInterface` is the standard query object passed to `getList()`. It encodes filters, sorting, and pagination.

### Object Hierarchy

```
SearchCriteriaInterface
|
+-- getFilterGroups(): FilterGroup[]
|       |
|       +-- FilterGroup (OR container)
|               |
|               +-- getFilters(): Filter[]
|                       |
|                       +-- Filter
|                               +-- getField()         e.g. 'price'
|                               +-- getValue()         e.g. '100'
|                               +-- getConditionType() e.g. 'gteq'
|
+-- getSortOrders(): SortOrder[]
|       |
|       +-- SortOrder
|               +-- getField()     e.g. 'name'
|               +-- getDirection() 'ASC' | 'DESC'
|
+-- getPageSize(): int    (items per page)
+-- getCurrentPage(): int (1-based page number)
```

### Filter Logic: AND vs OR

```
FilterGroups are combined with AND
Filters within a FilterGroup are combined with OR

Example:
  Group 1: [price >= 100]         (AND)
  Group 2: [color = 'red'         (OR)
             color = 'blue']

SQL equivalent:
  WHERE (price >= 100) AND (color = 'red' OR color = 'blue')
```

### Condition Types Reference

| Condition Type | SQL Equivalent | Example Value |
|---|---|---|
| `eq` | `= 'value'` | `'active'` |
| `neq` | `!= 'value'` | `'inactive'` |
| `like` | `LIKE '%value%'` | `'%shirt%'` |
| `nlike` | `NOT LIKE` | `'%test%'` |
| `in` | `IN (1,2,3)` | `'1,2,3'` |
| `nin` | `NOT IN` | `'4,5,6'` |
| `gt` | `> value` | `'100'` |
| `lt` | `< value` | `'50'` |
| `gteq` | `>= value` | `'100'` |
| `lteq` | `<= value` | `'200'` |
| `null` | `IS NULL` | (any) |
| `notnull` | `IS NOT NULL` | (any) |
| `finset` | `FIND_IN_SET(?, field)` | `'42'` |
| `from` | `>= value` (date range start) | `'YYYY-MM-DD'` |
| `to` | `<= value` (date range end) | `'YYYY-MM-DD'` |

> **Note:** `finset` is critical for **multiselect attributes** that store comma-separated option IDs in varchar. `FIND_IN_SET` finds a value within a comma-delimited string. Additional supported types include `regexp`, `nfinset` (NOT FIND_IN_SET), `seq`/`sneq` (string equal/not-equal). The full list is in `Magento\Framework\DB\Adapter\Pdo\Mysql::prepareSqlCondition()`.

### Building SearchCriteria with SearchCriteriaBuilder

```php
<?php

use Magento\Framework\Api\SearchCriteriaBuilder;
use Magento\Framework\Api\FilterBuilder;
use Magento\Framework\Api\SortOrderBuilder;

class WidgetSearch
{
    public function __construct(
        private readonly SearchCriteriaBuilder $searchCriteriaBuilder,
        private readonly FilterBuilder $filterBuilder,
        private readonly SortOrderBuilder $sortOrderBuilder,
        private readonly \Vendor\Module\Api\WidgetRepositoryInterface $widgetRepository,
    ) {}

    public function findActiveWidgetsInPriceRange(float $min, float $max): array
    {
        // --- Build individual filters ---

        // Filter: price >= $min
        $priceMinFilter = $this->filterBuilder
            ->setField('price')
            ->setValue($min)
            ->setConditionType('gteq')
            ->create();

        // Filter: price <= $max
        $priceMaxFilter = $this->filterBuilder
            ->setField('price')
            ->setValue($max)
            ->setConditionType('lteq')
            ->create();

        // Filter: is_active = 1
        $activeFilter = $this->filterBuilder
            ->setField('is_active')
            ->setValue(1)
            ->setConditionType('eq')
            ->create();

        // --- Build sort order ---
        $sortOrder = $this->sortOrderBuilder
            ->setField('name')
            ->setAscendingDirection()   // or ->setDescendingDirection()
            ->create();

        // --- Assemble SearchCriteria ---
        // addFilters([...]) puts filters into the SAME FilterGroup (OR logic)
        // Multiple addFilters() calls create separate FilterGroups (AND logic)
        $searchCriteria = $this->searchCriteriaBuilder
            ->addFilters([$priceMinFilter])  // Group 1: price >= min
            ->addFilters([$priceMaxFilter])  // Group 2: price <= max  (AND with group 1)
            ->addFilters([$activeFilter])    // Group 3: is_active = 1 (AND with groups 1+2)
            ->addSortOrder($sortOrder)
            ->setPageSize(20)
            ->setCurrentPage(1)
            ->create();

        $searchResults = $this->widgetRepository->getList($searchCriteria);

        return $searchResults->getItems();   // array of WidgetInterface
    }

    public function findByColorOrStatus(string $color, string $status): array
    {
        // Color filter
        $colorFilter = $this->filterBuilder
            ->setField('color')
            ->setValue($color)
            ->setConditionType('eq')
            ->create();

        // Status filter
        $statusFilter = $this->filterBuilder
            ->setField('status')
            ->setValue($status)
            ->setConditionType('eq')
            ->create();

        // SAME addFilters() call = OR logic between colorFilter and statusFilter
        $searchCriteria = $this->searchCriteriaBuilder
            ->addFilters([$colorFilter, $statusFilter])   // (color='red' OR status='enabled')
            ->create();

        return $this->widgetRepository->getList($searchCriteria)->getItems();
    }
}
```

> **Exam focus:**
> - **Same `addFilters()` call** = filters are in the same `FilterGroup` = **OR** logic
> - **Separate `addFilters()` calls** = different `FilterGroup`s = **AND** logic between groups
> - `SearchCriteriaBuilder` is **stateful** — call `->create()` to reset it after building

---

## 7. Repository Implementation

### Full Repository Implementation

```php
<?php
// Vendor/Module/Model/WidgetRepository.php

namespace Vendor\Module\Model;

use Magento\Framework\Api\SearchCriteriaInterface;
use Magento\Framework\Api\SearchCriteria\CollectionProcessorInterface;
use Magento\Framework\Api\ExtensionAttribute\JoinProcessorInterface;
use Magento\Framework\Exception\CouldNotDeleteException;
use Magento\Framework\Exception\CouldNotSaveException;
use Magento\Framework\Exception\NoSuchEntityException;
use Vendor\Module\Api\Data\WidgetInterface;
use Vendor\Module\Api\Data\WidgetInterfaceFactory;
use Vendor\Module\Api\Data\WidgetSearchResultsInterface;
use Vendor\Module\Api\Data\WidgetSearchResultsInterfaceFactory;
use Vendor\Module\Api\WidgetRepositoryInterface;
use Vendor\Module\Model\ResourceModel\Widget as WidgetResource;
use Vendor\Module\Model\ResourceModel\Widget\CollectionFactory;

class WidgetRepository implements WidgetRepositoryInterface
{
    /**
     * Identity cache: widgetId => WidgetInterface
     * Prevents redundant DB hits for the same ID within a request.
     *
     * @var array<int, WidgetInterface>
     */
    private array $cache = [];

    public function __construct(
        private readonly WidgetResource $resource,
        private readonly WidgetInterfaceFactory $widgetFactory,
        private readonly CollectionFactory $collectionFactory,
        private readonly WidgetSearchResultsInterfaceFactory $searchResultsFactory,
        private readonly CollectionProcessorInterface $collectionProcessor,
        private readonly JoinProcessorInterface $extensionAttributesJoinProcessor,
    ) {}

    // -------------------------------------------------------------------------
    // SAVE
    // -------------------------------------------------------------------------

    public function save(WidgetInterface $widget): WidgetInterface
    {
        try {
            $this->resource->save($widget);
        } catch (\Exception $e) {
            throw new CouldNotSaveException(
                __('Could not save widget: %1', $e->getMessage()),
                $e
            );
        }

        // Invalidate identity cache on save
        unset($this->cache[$widget->getId()]);

        return $widget;
    }

    // -------------------------------------------------------------------------
    // GET BY ID
    // -------------------------------------------------------------------------

    public function getById(int $widgetId): WidgetInterface
    {
        // Serve from identity cache if available
        if (isset($this->cache[$widgetId])) {
            return $this->cache[$widgetId];
        }

        $widget = $this->widgetFactory->create();
        $this->resource->load($widget, $widgetId);

        if (!$widget->getId()) {
            // MUST throw — never return null
            throw new NoSuchEntityException(
                __('Widget with id "%1" does not exist.', $widgetId)
            );
        }

        $this->cache[$widgetId] = $widget;

        return $widget;
    }

    // -------------------------------------------------------------------------
    // GET LIST
    // -------------------------------------------------------------------------

    public function getList(SearchCriteriaInterface $searchCriteria): WidgetSearchResultsInterface
    {
        $collection = $this->collectionFactory->create();

        // CRITICAL STEP: Process extension attribute joins BEFORE applying filters
        // Without this, extension attribute fields are unknown to the collection
        $this->extensionAttributesJoinProcessor->process($collection);

        // Apply filters, sort orders, pagination from SearchCriteria to collection
        $this->collectionProcessor->process($searchCriteria, $collection);

        // Build SearchResults object
        $searchResults = $this->searchResultsFactory->create();
        $searchResults->setSearchCriteria($searchCriteria);
        $searchResults->setItems($collection->getItems());
        $searchResults->setTotalCount($collection->getSize());

        return $searchResults;
    }

    // -------------------------------------------------------------------------
    // DELETE
    // -------------------------------------------------------------------------

    public function delete(WidgetInterface $widget): bool
    {
        try {
            unset($this->cache[$widget->getId()]);
            $this->resource->delete($widget);
        } catch (\Exception $e) {
            throw new CouldNotDeleteException(
                __('Could not delete widget: %1', $e->getMessage()),
                $e
            );
        }

        return true;
    }

    public function deleteById(int $widgetId): bool
    {
        return $this->delete($this->getById($widgetId));
    }
}
```

### SearchResults Object Structure

```php
<?php
// Vendor/Module/Api/Data/WidgetSearchResultsInterface.php

namespace Vendor\Module\Api\Data;

use Magento\Framework\Api\SearchResultsInterface;

/**
 * @api
 */
interface WidgetSearchResultsInterface extends SearchResultsInterface
{
    /**
     * @return \Vendor\Module\Api\Data\WidgetInterface[]
     */
    public function getItems(): array;

    /**
     * @param \Vendor\Module\Api\Data\WidgetInterface[] $items
     * @return $this
     */
    public function setItems(array $items): self;
}
```

> **Exam focus:**
> - `SearchResultsInterface::getItems()` returns an **array of DataInterface objects** — NOT a plain untyped array
> - `setTotalCount()` stores the **pre-pagination total** (used for REST API pagination headers)
> - `setSearchCriteria()` echoes back the criteria used (important for REST consumers)

---

## 8. Extension Attributes

Extension attributes allow **third-party modules to attach additional data** to existing entities without modifying the original module. They are the correct way to add fields to a DataInterface you don't own.

### extension_attributes.xml

```xml
<!-- Vendor/NewModule/etc/extension_attributes.xml -->
<config xmlns:xsi="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema-instance"
        xsi:noNamespaceSchemaLocation="urn:magento:framework:Api/etc/extension_attributes.xsd">

    <!--
        Extend the product entity with a warranty period field.
        The 'for' attribute must match the DataInterface fully-qualified class name.
    -->
    <extension_attributes for="Magento\Catalog\Api\Data\ProductInterface">

        <!-- Simple scalar attribute -->
        <attribute code="warranty_period" type="int"/>

        <!-- Complex attribute backed by a join to another table (illustrative example) -->
        <!-- NOTE: The real stock_item extension attribute in Magento_CatalogInventory does NOT
             use a <join> element — it only declares <resources> for ACL. The join syntax below
             is valid per extension_attributes.xsd and is used in test modules. -->
        <attribute code="custom_stock_data" type="Magento\CatalogInventory\Api\Data\StockItemInterface">
            <join reference_table="cataloginventory_stock_item"
                  reference_field="product_id"
                  join_on_field="entity_id">
                <field>qty</field>
                <field>is_in_stock</field>
            </join>
        </attribute>

    </extension_attributes>

</config>
```

### Generated Extension Interface

After running `bin/magento setup:di:compile`, Magento generates:

```php
<?php
// Generated: Magento\Catalog\Api\Data\ProductExtensionInterface (auto-generated)

namespace Magento\Catalog\Api\Data;

interface ProductExtensionInterface extends \Magento\Framework\Api\ExtensionAttributesInterface
{
    /**
     * @return int|null
     */
    public function getWarrantyPeriod(): ?int;

    /**
     * @param int $warrantyPeriod
     * @return $this
     */
    public function setWarrantyPeriod(int $warrantyPeriod): self;

    /**
     * @return \Magento\CatalogInventory\Api\Data\StockItemInterface|null
     */
    public function getStockItem(): ?\Magento\CatalogInventory\Api\Data\StockItemInterface;

    /**
     * @param \Magento\CatalogInventory\Api\Data\StockItemInterface $stockItem
     * @return $this
     */
    public function setStockItem(
        \Magento\CatalogInventory\Api\Data\StockItemInterface $stockItem
    ): self;
}
```

### Loading Extension Attributes via Plugin

Extension attributes are **not loaded automatically**. You must use a plugin on the repository's `getById()` (and `getList()`) methods:

```php
<?php
// Vendor/NewModule/Plugin/ProductRepositoryPlugin.php

namespace Vendor\NewModule\Plugin;

use Magento\Catalog\Api\Data\ProductInterface;
use Magento\Catalog\Api\ProductRepositoryInterface;
use Magento\Framework\Api\SearchCriteriaInterface;
use Vendor\NewModule\Api\WarrantyRepositoryInterface;

class ProductRepositoryPlugin
{
    public function __construct(
        private readonly WarrantyRepositoryInterface $warrantyRepository,
    ) {}

    /**
     * After plugin on getById — load and attach extension attributes.
     */
    public function afterGetById(
        ProductRepositoryInterface $subject,
        ProductInterface $product
    ): ProductInterface {
        return $this->attachWarranty($product);
    }

    /**
     * After plugin on getList — load extension attributes for each item.
     * NOTE: extensionAttributesJoinProcessor->process() in the repository
     * handles JOIN-based attributes. This plugin handles separate-query attributes.
     */
    public function afterGetList(
        ProductRepositoryInterface $subject,
        \Magento\Catalog\Api\Data\ProductSearchResultsInterface $searchResults
    ): \Magento\Catalog\Api\Data\ProductSearchResultsInterface {
        foreach ($searchResults->getItems() as $product) {
            $this->attachWarranty($product);
        }
        return $searchResults;
    }

    private function attachWarranty(ProductInterface $product): ProductInterface
    {
        $extensionAttributes = $product->getExtensionAttributes()
            ?? \Magento\Framework\App\ObjectManager::getInstance()
                ->create(\Magento\Catalog\Api\Data\ProductExtensionInterface::class);

        try {
            $warranty = $this->warrantyRepository->getByProductId((int) $product->getId());
            $extensionAttributes->setWarrantyPeriod($warranty->getPeriod());
        } catch (\Magento\Framework\Exception\NoSuchEntityException $e) {
            // No warranty for this product — that's fine
        }

        $product->setExtensionAttributes($extensionAttributes);

        return $product;
    }
}
```

```xml
<!-- Vendor/NewModule/etc/di.xml — register the plugin -->
<config>
    <type name="Magento\Catalog\Api\ProductRepositoryInterface">
        <plugin name="vendor_newmodule_product_extension_attributes"
                type="Vendor\NewModule\Plugin\ProductRepositoryPlugin"/>
    </type>
</config>
```

> **Exam focus:**
> - Extension attributes are in `etc/extension_attributes.xml`
> - **Generated** during `setup:di:compile` — never manually edit the generated files
> - Must be **manually loaded** via plugins on repository methods
> - `getExtensionAttributes()` can return `null` — always null-check and create if needed

---

## 9. Critical Gotchas

This section covers the highest-frequency exam traps around the repository pattern.

### Gotcha 1: getList() Does NOT Auto-Load Extension Attributes

```
Common Mistake:
  You define extension_attributes.xml with a <join> element.
  You call getList() and expect the join to happen automatically.
  The extension attributes are NULL on every item.

Root Cause:
  The join is only applied when extensionAttributesJoinProcessor->process()
  is explicitly called on the collection BEFORE executing the query.

Fix:
  In your repository's getList() implementation:

  $collection = $this->collectionFactory->create();

  // THIS LINE IS MANDATORY — without it, join-based extension attributes
  // are silently empty
  $this->extensionAttributesJoinProcessor->process($collection);

  $this->collectionProcessor->process($searchCriteria, $collection);
```

```php
// WRONG — extension attributes from joins will be missing
public function getList(SearchCriteriaInterface $searchCriteria): MySearchResultsInterface
{
    $collection = $this->collectionFactory->create();
    $this->collectionProcessor->process($searchCriteria, $collection);  // <-- join not set up
    // ...
}

// CORRECT
public function getList(SearchCriteriaInterface $searchCriteria): MySearchResultsInterface
{
    $collection = $this->collectionFactory->create();
    $this->extensionAttributesJoinProcessor->process($collection); // <-- JOIN first!
    $this->collectionProcessor->process($searchCriteria, $collection);
    // ...
}
```

> **Exam focus:** `extensionAttributesJoinProcessor->process()` **MUST be called before** `collectionProcessor->process()` in `getList()` to enable extension attribute joins.

---

### Gotcha 2: getById() Throws, Never Returns Null

```php
// WRONG — violates service contract
public function getById(int $id): ?WidgetInterface
{
    $widget = $this->widgetFactory->create();
    $this->resource->load($widget, $id);
    return $widget->getId() ? $widget : null;  // <-- NEVER do this
}

// CORRECT
public function getById(int $id): WidgetInterface
{
    $widget = $this->widgetFactory->create();
    $this->resource->load($widget, $id);

    if (!$widget->getId()) {
        throw new NoSuchEntityException(
            __('Widget with id "%1" does not exist.', $id)
        );
    }

    return $widget;
}
```

> **Exam focus:** Return type is `DataInterface`, **not** `?DataInterface`. Missing entities throw `NoSuchEntityException`. Callers must use try/catch.

---

### Gotcha 3: SearchResults::getItems() Returns DataInterface Array

```php
// getList() returns SearchResultsInterface, NOT an array

$results = $productRepository->getList($searchCriteria);

// WRONG — $results is a SearchResultsInterface object, not iterable directly
foreach ($results as $product) { /* TypeError */ }

// CORRECT — call getItems() to get the array of DataInterface objects
foreach ($results->getItems() as $product) {
    echo $product->getName();  // $product is ProductInterface
}

// Also available:
$totalCount  = $results->getTotalCount();   // total matching records (pre-pagination)
$criteria    = $results->getSearchCriteria(); // echoes back what was searched
```

> **Exam focus:** `getList()` returns `SearchResultsInterface`. You must call `->getItems()` to get the array. `getTotalCount()` returns the total records **before pagination** — not just the current page count.

---

### Gotcha 4: SearchCriteriaBuilder is Stateful

```php
// WRONG — builder state leaks between calls
$criteria1 = $this->searchCriteriaBuilder
    ->addFilter('status', 'enabled')
    ->create();

// At this point, ->create() should reset state, but if you reuse
// a shared builder instance without understanding the lifecycle, bugs appear.
// Always build completely fresh criteria per use.

// CORRECT — build full criteria then immediately call create()
$criteria = $this->searchCriteriaBuilder
    ->addFilter('status', 'enabled', 'eq')
    ->addFilter('price', '0', 'gt')
    ->setPageSize(10)
    ->setCurrentPage(1)
    ->create();  // resets internal state after this call
```

---

### Gotcha 5: addFilter() vs addFilters()

```php
// SearchCriteriaBuilder has two filter methods:

// addFilter($field, $value, $conditionType = 'eq')
// -- Convenience method, creates a single filter in its OWN FilterGroup
// -- Multiple addFilter() calls = AND logic

// addFilters(Filter[] $filters)
// -- Accepts an array of pre-built Filter objects in ONE FilterGroup
// -- Multiple filters in the same array = OR logic

// Example: (color='red' OR color='blue') AND (status='enabled')
$redFilter  = $this->filterBuilder->setField('color')->setValue('red')->setConditionType('eq')->create();
$blueFilter = $this->filterBuilder->setField('color')->setValue('blue')->setConditionType('eq')->create();

$criteria = $this->searchCriteriaBuilder
    ->addFilters([$redFilter, $blueFilter])   // OR group: color in (red, blue)
    ->addFilter('status', 'enabled', 'eq')    // AND: status = enabled
    ->create();
```

> **Exam focus:** `addFilters([filter1, filter2])` = **OR** within the group. Separate calls to `addFilters()` or `addFilter()` = **AND** between groups.

