## 1. Product Repository: ProductRepositoryInterface

### Overview

`Magento\Catalog\Api\ProductRepositoryInterface` is the **service contract** for CRUD operations on products. It lives in the Service Layer — above collections, below controllers.

```
+------------------+
|  Controller/CLI  |
+--------+---------+
         |
+--------v---------+
| ProductRepository|   <-- Service Contract (interface)
+--------+---------+
         |
+--------v---------+
|  Resource Model  |
+--------+---------+
         |
+--------v---------+
|    Database      |
+------------------+
```

### Interface Methods

| Method | Signature | Description |
|---|---|---|
| `get` | `get(string $sku, bool $editMode, int $storeId, bool $forceReload)` | Load by SKU |
| `getById` | `getById(int $productId, bool $editMode, int $storeId, bool $forceReload)` | Load by entity ID |
| `save` | `save(ProductInterface $product, bool $saveOptions = false)` | Create or update |
| `delete` | `delete(ProductInterface $product)` | Delete by object |
| `deleteById` | `deleteById(string $sku)` | Delete by SKU |
| `getList` | `getList(SearchCriteriaInterface $searchCriteria)` | Filtered collection |

### Code: Basic Repository Usage

```php
<?php
// Inject via constructor
use Magento\Catalog\Api\ProductRepositoryInterface;
use Magento\Framework\Api\SearchCriteriaBuilder;

class MyService
{
    public function __construct(
        private readonly ProductRepositoryInterface $productRepository,
        private readonly SearchCriteriaBuilder $searchCriteriaBuilder
    ) {}

    // Load by SKU
    public function getBySku(string $sku): \Magento\Catalog\Api\Data\ProductInterface
    {
        return $this->productRepository->get($sku);
    }

    // Load by ID
    public function getById(int $id): \Magento\Catalog\Api\Data\ProductInterface
    {
        return $this->productRepository->getById($id);
    }

    // getList with filter
    public function getInStock(): \Magento\Catalog\Api\Data\ProductSearchResultsInterface
    {
        $searchCriteria = $this->searchCriteriaBuilder
            ->addFilter('status', 1)
            ->addFilter('visibility', [2, 3, 4], 'in')
            ->setPageSize(20)
            ->setCurrentPage(1)
            ->create();

        return $this->productRepository->getList($searchCriteria);
    }
}
```

### The `get()` vs `getById()` Identity Map / Cache

Both methods use an **internal identity map (cache)**. Use `$forceReload = true` to bypass it:

```php
// Force fresh load — bypasses in-memory identity map
$product = $this->productRepository->get('my-sku', false, null, true);
$product = $this->productRepository->getById(42, false, null, true);
```

> **Exam focus:**
> - `get()` loads by **SKU**; `getById()` loads by **entity_id** — both share the same internal cache keyed by SKU AND id
> - `$forceReload = true` (4th parameter) is required if you modify and re-load a product in the same request
> - `getList()` returns a `ProductSearchResultsInterface` — iterate via `->getItems()`
> - The repository respects **store scope** via the `$storeId` parameter; omitting it uses the current store

### SearchCriteria Deep Dive

```php
use Magento\Framework\Api\SearchCriteriaBuilder;
use Magento\Framework\Api\FilterBuilder;
use Magento\Framework\Api\SortOrderBuilder;

// Building a complex search criteria
$searchCriteria = $this->searchCriteriaBuilder
    ->addFilter('type_id', 'simple')          // AND filter
    ->addFilter('price', 100, 'lteq')         // price <= 100
    ->addFilter('sku', ['PROD-1','PROD-2'], 'in')
    ->setPageSize(50)
    ->setCurrentPage(1)
    ->create();

// OR filters require FilterGroups directly
$filter1 = $this->filterBuilder->setField('status')->setValue(1)->setConditionType('eq')->create();
$filter2 = $this->filterBuilder->setField('visibility')->setValue(4)->setConditionType('eq')->create();

// Filters in SAME group = OR; different groups = AND
$searchCriteria = $this->searchCriteriaBuilder
    ->addFilters([$filter1, $filter2])  // OR within group
    ->create();
```

> **Exam focus:** Filters added via `addFilter()` to the *same* builder call are **ANDed**. To create OR conditions, build separate `Filter` objects and pass them in the same `FilterGroup`.

