## 3. Category Repository: CategoryRepositoryInterface

### Interface Methods

```php
namespace Magento\Catalog\Api;

interface CategoryRepositoryInterface
{
    public function get(int $categoryId, int $storeId = null): CategoryInterface;
    public function save(CategoryInterface $category): CategoryInterface;
    public function delete(CategoryInterface $category): bool;
    public function deleteByIdentifier(int $categoryId): bool;
}
```

### Creating and Saving Categories

```php
<?php
use Magento\Catalog\Api\CategoryRepositoryInterface;
use Magento\Catalog\Api\Data\CategoryInterfaceFactory;

class CategoryOperations
{
    public function __construct(
        private readonly CategoryRepositoryInterface $categoryRepository,
        private readonly CategoryInterfaceFactory $categoryFactory
    ) {}

    public function createCategory(int $parentId, string $name): void
    {
        $category = $this->categoryFactory->create();
        $category->setName($name);
        $category->setParentId($parentId);
        $category->setIsActive(true);
        $category->setIncludeInMenu(true);
        $category->setUrlKey(strtolower(str_replace(' ', '-', $name)));
        $category->setIsAnchor(true); // Show products from sub-categories

        $this->categoryRepository->save($category);
    }

    public function loadCategory(int $id): \Magento\Catalog\Api\Data\CategoryInterface
    {
        return $this->categoryRepository->get($id);
    }
}
```

> **Exam focus:**
> - `CategoryRepositoryInterface` does **not** have a `getList()` method — use `CategoryManagementInterface` for tree traversal
> - `setIsAnchor(true)` makes a category show products from child categories in collections
> - `setParentId()` determines position in the category tree — Magento recalculates `path` and `level` on save
> - Category IDs 1 (Root of Roots) and 2 (Default Category) are Magento system categories

