## 5. Collection Usage: ProductCollection

### Overview

While the Repository is preferred for service-layer code, `ProductCollection` is still heavily used for frontend/performance-sensitive listing scenarios.

```php
<?php
use Magento\Catalog\Model\ResourceModel\Product\CollectionFactory;
use Magento\Catalog\Model\Product\Visibility;

class ProductCollectionService
{
    public function __construct(
        private readonly CollectionFactory $productCollectionFactory,
        private readonly Visibility $productVisibility
    ) {}

    public function getProductCollection(): \Magento\Catalog\Model\ResourceModel\Product\Collection
    {
        $collection = $this->productCollectionFactory->create();

        // Select specific attributes (EAV columns)
        $collection->addAttributeToSelect('name');
        $collection->addAttributeToSelect('price');
        $collection->addAttributeToSelect('thumbnail');
        $collection->addAttributeToSelect('*'); // All attributes (expensive!)

        // Filter by attribute value
        $collection->addAttributeToFilter('status', 1);
        $collection->addAttributeToFilter('price', ['lteq' => 100]);
        $collection->addAttributeToFilter('sku', ['like' => 'PROD-%']);

        // Filter by multiple values (IN condition)
        $collection->addAttributeToFilter('type_id', ['in' => ['simple', 'configurable']]);

        // OR condition using array of conditions
        $collection->addAttributeToFilter([
            ['attribute' => 'color', 'eq' => 'Red'],
            ['attribute' => 'color', 'eq' => 'Blue'],
        ]);

        // Visibility filter (uses index table)
        $collection->addFieldToFilter(
            'visibility',
            ['in' => $this->productVisibility->getVisibleInSiteIds()]
        );

        return $collection;
    }
}
```

### `addAttributeToSelect` vs `addFieldToFilter` vs `addAttributeToFilter`

| Method | Applies To | Column Source |
|---|---|---|
| `addAttributeToSelect` | EAV attributes | Joins `catalog_product_entity_*` tables |
| `addAttributeToFilter` | EAV attributes | Filters on joined EAV value tables |
| `addFieldToFilter` | Flat/static columns | Filters directly on main table column |

```php
// addAttributeToFilter with condition types
$collection->addAttributeToFilter('price', ['gt' => 10]);       // >
$collection->addAttributeToFilter('price', ['lt' => 100]);      // <
$collection->addAttributeToFilter('price', ['gteq' => 10]);     // >=
$collection->addAttributeToFilter('price', ['lteq' => 100]);    // <=
$collection->addAttributeToFilter('price', ['eq' => 50]);       // =
$collection->addAttributeToFilter('price', ['neq' => 50]);      // !=
$collection->addAttributeToFilter('name', ['like' => '%foo%']); // LIKE
$collection->addAttributeToFilter('name', ['notnull' => true]); // IS NOT NULL
$collection->addAttributeToFilter('name', ['null' => true]);    // IS NULL
$collection->addAttributeToFilter('id', ['in' => [1,2,3]]);     // IN
$collection->addAttributeToFilter('id', ['nin' => [1,2,3]]);    // NOT IN
```

### `addCategoryFilter`

```php
<?php
use Magento\Catalog\Model\Category;

// Filter collection by a category
// This uses catalog_category_product_index for performance
$collection->addCategoryFilter($categoryObject);

// Alternatively — includes anchor categories (subcategory products)
// addCategoryFilter handles anchor logic internally
$category = $this->categoryRepository->get(5);
$collection->addCategoryFilter($category);

// For custom joins:
$collection->joinTable(
    'catalog_category_product',
    'product_id = entity_id',
    ['category_id'],
    '`at_category_id`.`category_id` = ' . $categoryId
);
```

> **Exam focus:**
> - `addCategoryFilter()` uses `catalog_category_product_index` — requires reindex to be current
> - If the category `is_anchor = 1`, the index includes products from child categories automatically
> - **Flat catalog** (when enabled) changes `addAttributeToFilter`/`addAttributeToSelect` to query `catalog_product_flat_X` tables instead of EAV — this can break custom queries that assume EAV joins

### Pagination and Ordering

```php
$collection->setPageSize(20);
$collection->setCurPage(1);
$collection->addAttributeToSort('price', 'ASC');
$collection->addAttributeToSort('name', 'DESC');

// Get total count without loading all items
$totalCount = $collection->getSize();

// Load and iterate
foreach ($collection as $product) {
    echo $product->getName() . ': ' . $product->getPrice();
}
```

