## 7. Product Media: Gallery Entries & Image Roles

### Image Roles

| Role | Code | Description |
|---|---|---|
| Base Image | `image` | Main product image |
| Small Image | `small_image` | Used in product listings |
| Thumbnail | `thumbnail` | Cart, related products |
| Swatch Image | `swatch_image` | Color/image swatches |

### MediaGalleryEntryInterface

```php
namespace Magento\Catalog\Api\Data;

interface ProductAttributeMediaGalleryEntryInterface
{
    public function getId(): int;
    public function getMediaType(): string;    // 'image' or 'external-video'
    public function getLabel(): string;        // Alt text
    public function getPosition(): int;        // Sort order
    public function isDisabled(): bool;        // Hidden from gallery
    public function getTypes(): array;         // ['image', 'small_image', 'thumbnail']
    public function getFile(): string;         // Path: /a/b/product.jpg
    public function getContent(): MediaGalleryEntryContentInterface; // For upload
}
```

### Reading Gallery Entries

```php
<?php
use Magento\Catalog\Api\ProductRepositoryInterface;

$product = $this->productRepository->get('MY-SKU');
$mediaGalleryEntries = $product->getMediaGalleryEntries();

foreach ($mediaGalleryEntries as $entry) {
    echo 'File: ' . $entry->getFile() . PHP_EOL;
    echo 'Label: ' . $entry->getLabel() . PHP_EOL;
    echo 'Types: ' . implode(', ', $entry->getTypes()) . PHP_EOL;
    echo 'Position: ' . $entry->getPosition() . PHP_EOL;
    echo 'Disabled: ' . ($entry->isDisabled() ? 'yes' : 'no') . PHP_EOL;
}
```

### Adding Images Programmatically

```php
<?php
use Magento\Catalog\Api\Data\ProductAttributeMediaGalleryEntryInterfaceFactory;
use Magento\Catalog\Api\Data\ProductAttributeMediaGalleryEntryContentInterfaceFactory;

class AddProductImage
{
    public function __construct(
        private readonly ProductRepositoryInterface $productRepository,
        private readonly ProductAttributeMediaGalleryEntryInterfaceFactory $galleryEntryFactory,
        private readonly ProductAttributeMediaGalleryEntryContentInterfaceFactory $galleryEntryContentFactory
    ) {}

    public function addImage(string $sku, string $imagePath): void
    {
        $product = $this->productRepository->get($sku);

        // Read file and base64 encode
        $imageContent = base64_encode(file_get_contents($imagePath));
        $mimeType = mime_content_type($imagePath); // e.g., 'image/jpeg'

        // Create content object (for new uploads)
        $content = $this->galleryEntryContentFactory->create();
        $content->setBase64EncodedData($imageContent);
        $content->setType($mimeType);
        $content->setName(basename($imagePath));

        // Create gallery entry
        $entry = $this->galleryEntryFactory->create();
        $entry->setMediaType('image');
        $entry->setLabel('Product Image');
        $entry->setPosition(1);
        $entry->setDisabled(false);
        $entry->setTypes(['image', 'small_image', 'thumbnail']); // Assign roles
        $entry->setContent($content);

        // Append to existing entries
        $entries = $product->getMediaGalleryEntries() ?? [];
        $entries[] = $entry;
        $product->setMediaGalleryEntries($entries);

        $this->productRepository->save($product);
    }
}
```

### ProductGalleryManagement API

```php
namespace Magento\Catalog\Api;

interface ProductAttributeMediaGalleryManagementInterface
{
    public function create(string $sku, MediaGalleryEntryInterface $entry): int; // Returns entry ID
    public function update(string $sku, MediaGalleryEntryInterface $entry): bool;
    public function remove(string $sku, int $entryId): bool;
    public function getList(string $sku): array;
}
```

> **Exam focus:**
> - Image roles (`image`, `small_image`, `thumbnail`, `swatch_image`) are stored as **EAV varchar attributes** in `catalog_product_entity_varchar` — each role is a separate attribute whose value is the file path (e.g., `/a/b/product.jpg`). The `catalog_product_entity_media_gallery_value` table stores gallery metadata (label, position, disabled) but NOT role assignments
> - A product can have **one file** assigned to **multiple roles** simultaneously
> - `setTypes([])` with an empty array removes all role assignments from an entry
> - The actual image files live in `pub/media/catalog/product/` with a two-level directory structure (e.g., `/a/b/filename.jpg`)
> - `isDisabled(true)` hides the image from the gallery but **does not delete** the file

