## 8. Tricky Concepts & Gotchas

### Tricky #1: Configurable Products — Children NOT Embedded

This is the **most common exam trap** with configurable products.

```
ProductRepository::get('CONF-SKU')
        |
        v
  Configurable Product
  - getSku() => 'CONF-SKU'
  - getTypeId() => 'configurable'
  - getExtensionAttributes()->getConfigurableProductLinks() => [ID1, ID2, ...]
        |
        |  !!!  Child products are NOT embedded in the product object  !!!
        |
        v
  You must call getList() or ConfigurableType::getUsedProducts() separately
```

```php
<?php
use Magento\Catalog\Api\ProductRepositoryInterface;
use Magento\Framework\Api\SearchCriteriaBuilder;
use Magento\ConfigurableProduct\Model\ResourceModel\Product\Type\Configurable as ConfigurableResource;

class LoadConfigurableWithChildren
{
    public function __construct(
        private readonly ProductRepositoryInterface $productRepository,
        private readonly SearchCriteriaBuilder $searchCriteriaBuilder,
        private readonly ConfigurableResource $configurableResource
    ) {}

    public function getChildrenViaRepository(string $parentSku): array
    {
        // Load parent
        $parent = $this->productRepository->get($parentSku);

        // Get child IDs from extension attributes
        $childIds = $parent->getExtensionAttributes()
                           ->getConfigurableProductLinks();
        // $childIds = [42, 43, 44] — entity IDs of children

        // Must do a SEPARATE getList() call to load child products
        $searchCriteria = $this->searchCriteriaBuilder
            ->addFilter('entity_id', $childIds, 'in')
            ->create();

        $result = $this->productRepository->getList($searchCriteria);
        return $result->getItems(); // Indexed by SKU
    }

    public function getChildrenViaModel(string $parentSku): array
    {
        $parent = $this->productRepository->get($parentSku);

        // Alternative: use configurable type model
        /** @var \Magento\Catalog\Model\Product $parentModel */
        $parentModel = $parent; // Product implements ProductInterface
        return $parentModel->getTypeInstance()->getUsedProducts($parentModel);
    }
}
```

> **Exam focus:**
> - Calling `$configurableProduct->getExtensionAttributes()->getConfigurableProductLinks()` returns an **array of child entity IDs**, NOT product objects
> - A **separate** `getList()` (or `getUsedProducts()`) call is required to load child data
> - `getUsedProducts()` returns `\Magento\Catalog\Model\Product[]` (model objects), uses cache internally
> - `getConfigurableProductOptions()` gives you the configurable attribute configuration (not child products)

### Tricky #2: Category Flat Tables

```
Flat Catalog ENABLED:                   Flat Catalog DISABLED (default):

catalog_product_flat_1 (store 1)        catalog_product_entity (main)
catalog_product_flat_2 (store 2)        + EAV tables:
                                          catalog_product_entity_varchar
These are denormalized tables             catalog_product_entity_int
pre-joining all attributes                catalog_product_entity_decimal
                                          catalog_product_entity_text
                                          catalog_product_entity_datetime
```

```php
// Check if flat is enabled programmatically
use Magento\Catalog\Model\Indexer\Product\Flat\State;

$flatState = $objectManager->get(State::class);
if ($flatState->isFlatEnabled()) {
    // addAttributeToFilter queries catalog_product_flat_X
    // Custom EAV joins will fail if attribute not in flat table!
}

// Check via config
// Note: The constant is Magento\Catalog\Model\Indexer\Product\Flat\State::INDEXER_ENABLED_XML_PATH
// which resolves to 'catalog/frontend/flat_catalog_product'
$isFlat = $scopeConfig->getValue(
    \Magento\Catalog\Model\Indexer\Product\Flat\State::INDEXER_ENABLED_XML_PATH,
    \Magento\Store\Model\ScopeInterface::SCOPE_STORE
);
```

**Impact on Collection Queries:**

| Operation | Flat Disabled | Flat Enabled |
|---|---|---|
| `addAttributeToSelect('name')` | Joins `catalog_product_entity_varchar` | Reads flat table column |
| `addAttributeToFilter('color',...)` | Joins EAV option table | Reads flat column directly |
| Custom `joinTable()` with EAV | Works | **May fail** if attribute not indexed in flat |
| `getSize()` | EAV subquery | Fast flat query |

> **Exam focus:**
> - Flat catalog is **disabled by default** in Magento 2 cloud/commerce; must be explicitly enabled
> - When flat is enabled, the flat table must be **reindexed** for changes to appear
> - Category flat (`catalog_category_flat`) is separate from product flat
> - Flat tables are **per store** — `catalog_product_flat_1`, `catalog_product_flat_2`, etc.
> - Custom attributes added after flat index creation need a **full reindex** to appear in flat tables

### Tricky #3: Store Scope & Repository

```php
// Loading in admin context (store ID = 0) returns GLOBAL scope values
$product = $this->productRepository->get('SKU', false, 0);

// Loading in store context returns store-overridden values
$product = $this->productRepository->get('SKU', false, 1); // Store 1

// editMode = true loads admin values regardless of store
$product = $this->productRepository->get('SKU', true, 1);
```

### Tricky #4: Category `getTree()` Depth

```php
// getTree(null) starts from the configured root category
// getTree(1) starts from "Root Catalog" (parent of all roots)
// getTree(2) starts from "Default Category"

// Depth examples:
$tree = $management->getTree(2, 0); // Root only, no children
$tree = $management->getTree(2, 1); // Root + immediate children
$tree = $management->getTree(2, 2); // Root + 2 levels deep
$tree = $management->getTree(2, null); // Full tree (unlimited)
```

