echo PHP_EOL . '=== SCRIPT COMPLETE ===' . PHP_EOL;
```

### Expected Output Structure

```
=== CONFIGURABLE PRODUCT ===
SKU:         MH01
Name:        Chaz Kangeroo Hoodie
Type:        configurable
Entity ID:   67
Status:      1
Visibility:  4

=== CONFIGURABLE OPTIONS (Attribute Configuration) ===
Attribute: Color (ID: 93)
  - Option Value Index: 49
  - Option Value Index: 50
  ...
Attribute: Size (ID: 144)
  - Option Value Index: 167
  ...

=== CHILD PRODUCT IDs ===
IDs: 68, 69, 70, 71, 72, ...
Count: 12

=== METHOD 1: Load Children via Repository::getList() ===
Children found: 12

  SKU:        MH01-XS-Black
  Name:       Chaz Kangeroo Hoodie-XS-Black
  Type:       simple
  Price:      52.00
  Status:     1
  Color:      49
  Size:       167
  Images:     1
  ...
```

### Key Differences: `getList()` vs `getUsedProducts()`

| Aspect | `getList()` | `getUsedProducts()` |
|---|---|---|
| Returns | `ProductInterface[]` (repository objects) | `Product[]` (model objects) |
| Extension Attributes | Fully loaded | Not always loaded |
| Cache | Repository identity map | Type instance cache |
| Scope | Respects `SearchCriteria` store scope | Current store |
| Custom Attributes | Via `getCustomAttribute()` | Via `getData()` or getter |
| Use Case | Service layer, API responses | Frontend rendering, type logic |

