## 1. Quote & Cart Operations

### 1.1 Architecture Overview

```
Customer Request
      |
      v
CartManagementInterface        <-- Orchestrates the full cart lifecycle
      |
      +---> CartRepositoryInterface      <-- Persistence layer (load/save quote)
      |
      +---> CartItemRepositoryInterface  <-- Individual line-item management
      |
      v
  Quote (Mage\Quote\Model\Quote)
      |
      +---> Quote\Address (billing / shipping)
      +---> Quote\Item[]
      +---> Quote\Payment
```

### 1.2 CartManagementInterface

**Namespace:** `Magento\Quote\Api\CartManagementInterface`

| Method | Signature | Returns | Description |
|---|---|---|---|
| `createEmptyCart` | `createEmptyCart()` | `int` (cart/quote ID) | Creates a new empty quote for a guest |
| `createEmptyCartForCustomer` | `createEmptyCartForCustomer(int $customerId)` | `int` | Creates a quote assigned to a logged-in customer |
| `assignCustomer` | `assignCustomer(int $cartId, int $customerId, int $storeId)` | `bool` | Merges a guest cart into a customer cart |
| `placeOrder` | `placeOrder(int $cartId, PaymentInterface $paymentMethod = null)` | `int` (Order ID) | Validates and converts quote to order |
| `getCartForCustomer` | `getCartForCustomer(int $customerId)` | `CartInterface` | Returns active cart for customer |

**Exam focus:**
- `createEmptyCart()` is for **guests**; `createEmptyCartForCustomer()` is for **authenticated customers**
- `placeOrder()` returns the **Order ID (integer)**, not the order object
- `placeOrder()` triggers the full validation pipeline — payment, shipping, inventory, addresses

#### 1.2.1 Guest Cart Creation Example

```php
<?php
declare(strict_types=1);

use Magento\Quote\Api\CartManagementInterface;
use Magento\Quote\Api\CartRepositoryInterface;
use Magento\Quote\Api\Data\CartInterface;

class GuestCartExample
{
    public function __construct(
        private readonly CartManagementInterface $cartManagement,
        private readonly CartRepositoryInterface $cartRepository,
    ) {}

    public function createGuestCart(): CartInterface
    {
        // Returns the new quote (cart) ID as an integer
        $cartId = $this->cartManagement->createEmptyCart();

        // Load the cart object from the repository
        return $this->cartRepository->get($cartId);
    }
}
```

#### 1.2.2 Customer Cart Creation Example

```php
<?php
declare(strict_types=1);

use Magento\Quote\Api\CartManagementInterface;
use Magento\Quote\Api\CartRepositoryInterface;

class CustomerCartExample
{
    public function __construct(
        private readonly CartManagementInterface $cartManagement,
        private readonly CartRepositoryInterface $cartRepository,
    ) {}

    public function createOrGetCustomerCart(int $customerId): \Magento\Quote\Api\Data\CartInterface
    {
        try {
            // Try to get the existing active cart first
            return $this->cartManagement->getCartForCustomer($customerId);
        } catch (\Magento\Framework\Exception\NoSuchEntityException $e) {
            // No active cart — create one
            $cartId = $this->cartManagement->createEmptyCartForCustomer($customerId);
            return $this->cartRepository->get($cartId);
        }
    }
}
```

---

### 1.3 CartItemRepositoryInterface

**Namespace:** `Magento\Quote\Api\CartItemRepositoryInterface`

Manages individual **line items** within a quote without touching the quote itself.

| Method | Signature | Description |
|---|---|---|
| `getList` | `getList(int $cartId)` | Returns `CartItemInterface[]` for a cart |
| `save` | `save(CartItemInterface $cartItem)` | Adds or updates a line item |
| `deleteById` | `deleteById(int $cartId, int $itemId)` | Removes an item by its item ID |

**Exam focus:**
- `CartItemRepositoryInterface::save()` is the programmatic equivalent of "Add to Cart"
- The `CartItemInterface` requires `quoteId`, `sku`, `qty`, and `productType`
- For **configurable products**, you must pass `productOption` with the selected option values

```php
<?php
declare(strict_types=1);

use Magento\Quote\Api\CartItemRepositoryInterface;
use Magento\Quote\Api\Data\CartItemInterfaceFactory;

class AddItemToCartExample
{
    public function __construct(
        private readonly CartItemRepositoryInterface $cartItemRepository,
        private readonly CartItemInterfaceFactory $cartItemFactory,
    ) {}

    public function addSimpleProduct(int $cartId, string $sku, float $qty): void
    {
        $cartItem = $this->cartItemFactory->create();
        $cartItem->setQuoteId($cartId);
        $cartItem->setSku($sku);
        $cartItem->setQty($qty);
        $cartItem->setProductType(\Magento\Catalog\Model\Product\Type::TYPE_SIMPLE);

        $this->cartItemRepository->save($cartItem);
    }
}
```

