## 2. Custom Total Model

### 2.1 What Is a Total Model?

Total models calculate **price components** added to or subtracted from the order total. Examples: `subtotal`, `shipping`, `tax`, `discount`, `grand_total`.

All custom totals extend `Magento\Quote\Model\Quote\Address\Total\AbstractTotal`.

**Exam focus:**
- The `collect()` method is **mandatory** — it computes the total and applies it to the address
- The `fetch()` method controls how the total appears in the **cart/checkout totals block** (display layer)
- Total models are registered in `di.xml` and configured with a **sort order** that controls calculation sequence

### 2.2 Execution Flow

```
Quote::collectTotals()
        |
        v
Address::collectTotals()
        |
        v
TotalCollector::collect($quote, $address)
        |
        +---> foreach registered Total models (sorted by sortOrder):
              |
              +---> AbstractTotal::collect($quote, $shippingAssignment, $total)
                        |
                        +---> $total->addTotalAmount($code, $amount)
                        +---> $total->addBaseTotalAmount($code, $baseAmount)
                        +---> $address->setGrandTotal($address->getGrandTotal() + $amount)
```

### 2.3 Implementing a Custom Total

#### Step 1: Create the Total Model Class

```php
<?php
declare(strict_types=1);

namespace Vendor\Module\Model\Quote\Address\Total;

use Magento\Framework\Phrase;
use Magento\Quote\Api\Data\ShippingAssignmentInterface;
use Magento\Quote\Model\Quote;
use Magento\Quote\Model\Quote\Address\Total;
use Magento\Quote\Model\Quote\Address\Total\AbstractTotal;

class CustomFee extends AbstractTotal
{
    private const FEE_AMOUNT = 5.00;
    private const TOTAL_CODE = 'custom_fee';

    public function __construct()
    {
        $this->setCode(self::TOTAL_CODE);
    }

    /**
     * Collect the custom total and add to address totals.
     * This method MUST add the amount to the Total object AND update the address.
     */
    public function collect(
        Quote $quote,
        ShippingAssignmentInterface $shippingAssignment,
        Total $total
    ): static {
        // Always call parent first — resets the total for recalculation
        parent::collect($quote, $shippingAssignment, $total);

        // Guard: only process for the shipping address items
        $items = $shippingAssignment->getItems();
        if (!count($items)) {
            return $this;
        }

        $feeAmount = self::FEE_AMOUNT;
        $baseFeeAmount = self::FEE_AMOUNT; // Apply currency conversion logic here if needed

        // Step 1: Add to the Total aggregator (tracks per-total amounts)
        $total->addTotalAmount($this->getCode(), $feeAmount);
        $total->addBaseTotalAmount($this->getCode(), $baseFeeAmount);

        // Step 2: Set the custom attribute on the quote for persistence
        $quote->setData('custom_fee', $feeAmount);
        $quote->setData('base_custom_fee', $baseFeeAmount);

        return $this;
    }

    /**
     * Fetch controls rendering in totals block.
     * Return null to hide, or an array to display.
     */
    public function fetch(Quote $quote, Total $total): array
    {
        return [
            'code'  => $this->getCode(),
            'title' => $this->getLabel(),
            'value' => $total->getTotalAmount($this->getCode()),
        ];
    }

    public function getLabel(): Phrase
    {
        return __('Custom Fee');
    }
}
```

**Exam focus:**
- `parent::collect()` **resets** the current total amount — always call it first
- `$total->addTotalAmount(code, amount)` adds to the **address-level total tracker**
- You must also **set the value on the quote** (`$quote->setData(...)`) for the amount to persist to the order
- `$shippingAssignment->getItems()` — if empty, you are processing the billing address; skip to avoid double-counting

#### Step 2: Register in `sales.xml`

Custom totals are registered in `sales.xml` (NOT `di.xml`). There is no `TotalFactory` class — Magento uses `Magento\Quote\Model\Quote\Address\Total\Collector` (extending `Magento\Sales\Model\Config\Ordered`) to load totals from `sales.xml`.

```xml
<!-- app/code/Vendor/Module/etc/sales.xml -->
<?xml version="1.0"?>
<config xmlns:xsi="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema-instance"
        xsi:noNamespaceSchemaLocation="urn:magento:module:Magento_Sales:etc/sales.xsd">

    <section name="quote">
        <group name="totals">
            <item name="custom_fee" instance="Vendor\Module\Model\Quote\Address\Total\CustomFee"
                  sort_order="500"/>
        </group>
    </section>

</config>
```

**Exam focus:**
- `sort_order` determines **calculation sequence** — `subtotal=100`, `tax_subtotal=200`, `discount=300`, `shipping=350`, `tax_shipping=375`, `shipping_discount=400`, `tax=450`, `grand_total=550`
- Set your custom total's sort order **before** `grand_total` (550) but **after** anything it depends on
- The `instance` attribute points to your total class; `name` is the unique total code

