## 3. Custom Checkout Step

### 3.1 Architecture Overview

A custom checkout step requires **three layers** working together:

```
+---------------------+     +----------------------+     +----------------------+
|  checkout_index_    |     |  JS Component        |     |  PHP LayoutProcessor |
|  index.xml          | --> |  (KnockoutJS/Mage UI) | --> |  (adds step to       |
|  (layout XML)       |     |  renders the step UI  |     |   steps config array)|
+---------------------+     +----------------------+     +----------------------+
```

**Exam focus:**
- Both the **JS component** AND the **PHP LayoutProcessor** are required for a custom step
- The layout XML (`checkout_index_index.xml`) is where you **inject** your LayoutProcessor
- The JS component must implement `navigate()` and be registered in `checkout_index_index.xml` via the steps configuration path

### 3.2 PHP LayoutProcessor

The PHP LayoutProcessor adds your step's configuration to the JavaScript layout array passed to the checkout UI.

```php
<?php
declare(strict_types=1);

namespace Vendor\Module\Block\Checkout;

use Magento\Checkout\Block\Checkout\LayoutProcessorInterface;

class CustomStepLayoutProcessor implements LayoutProcessorInterface
{
    /**
     * Process the checkout layout and inject the custom step.
     *
     * @param array $jsLayout The existing JS layout configuration array
     * @return array Modified JS layout
     */
    public function process(array $jsLayout): array
    {
        $jsLayout['components']['checkout']['children']['steps']['children']['custom-step'] = [
            'component'  => 'Vendor_Module/js/view/checkout/custom-step',
            'sortOrder'  => '2',                // Controls position between Shipping (1) and Payment (2)
            'children'   => [],
            'config'     => [
                'title' => __('Custom Step'),
            ],
        ];

        return $jsLayout;
    }
}
```

### 3.3 Register the LayoutProcessor via `di.xml`

LayoutProcessors are registered via **`di.xml`** as constructor arguments on the `Onepage` block (NOT via layout XML). The `layoutProcessors` parameter is a named constructor argument, not part of the `$data` array, so layout XML `<arguments>` cannot inject it.

```xml
<!-- app/code/Vendor/Module/etc/frontend/di.xml -->
<?xml version="1.0"?>
<config xmlns:xsi="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema-instance"
        xsi:noNamespaceSchemaLocation="urn:magento:framework:ObjectManager/etc/config.xsd">

    <type name="Magento\Checkout\Block\Onepage">
        <arguments>
            <argument name="layoutProcessors" xsi:type="array">
                <item name="customStepProcessor" xsi:type="object">
                    Vendor\Module\Block\Checkout\CustomStepLayoutProcessor
                </item>
            </argument>
        </arguments>
    </type>

</config>
```

**Exam focus:**
- The block is **`Magento\Checkout\Block\Onepage`** — it accepts `layoutProcessors` as a constructor argument
- Magento's own LayoutProcessors are registered in `vendor/magento/module-checkout/etc/frontend/di.xml`
- Layout processors implement `Magento\Checkout\Block\Checkout\LayoutProcessorInterface`
- The LayoutProcessor's `process()` method receives the **full** JS layout array and must return the modified version

### 3.4 JavaScript Component

```javascript
// app/code/Vendor/Module/view/frontend/web/js/view/checkout/custom-step.js
define([
    'ko',
    'uiComponent',
    'underscore',
    'Magento_Checkout/js/model/step-navigator'
], function (ko, Component, _, stepNavigator) {
    'use strict';

    /**
     * Custom checkout step component.
     * Must be registered with stepNavigator to appear in the checkout progress bar.
     */
    return Component.extend({
        defaults: {
            template: 'Vendor_Module/checkout/custom-step'
        },

        // Unique code for this step — used by stepNavigator
        isVisible: ko.observable(false),
        stepCode: 'custom-step',
        stepTitle: 'Custom Step',

        /** Called by Magento_Checkout/js/view/progress-bar automatically */
        initialize: function () {
            this._super();

            // Register step with the navigator
            // sortOrder determines position in the flow (1=shipping, 2=payment by default)
            stepNavigator.registerStep(
                this.stepCode,      // code
                null,               // alias (null uses code)
                this.stepTitle,     // title (shown in progress bar)
                this.isVisible,     // KO observable — controls visibility
                _.bind(this.navigate, this),  // navigate callback
                15                  // sortOrder (between shipping=10 and payment=20)
            );

            return this;
        },

        /**
         * Navigate to this step.
         * Called by stepNavigator when the user clicks on this step.
         */
        navigate: function () {
            this.isVisible(true);
        },

        /**
         * Navigate to the next step.
         */
        navigateToNextStep: function () {
            stepNavigator.next();
        }
    });
});
```

### 3.5 KnockoutJS Template

```html
<!-- app/code/Vendor/Module/view/frontend/web/template/checkout/custom-step.html -->
<li id="custom-step" data-bind="fadeVisible: isVisible">
    <div class="step-title" data-bind="i18n: 'Custom Step'" data-role="title"></div>
    <div id="checkout-step-custom"
         class="step-content"
         data-role="content"
         data-bind="visible: isVisible">

        <form data-bind="submit: navigateToNextStep" novalidate="novalidate">
            <div class="custom-step-content">
                <!-- Your custom step fields here -->
                <p data-bind="i18n: 'This is a custom checkout step.'"></p>
            </div>

            <div class="actions-toolbar">
                <div class="primary">
                    <button data-role="opc-continue"
                            type="submit"
                            class="button action continue primary">
                        <span data-bind="i18n: 'Next'"></span>
                    </button>
                </div>
            </div>
        </form>

    </div>
</li>
```

**Exam focus:**
- `stepNavigator.registerStep()` **must** be called in `initialize()` — this is what makes the step appear in the checkout progress bar
- `isVisible` must be a **KnockoutJS observable** (`ko.observable(false)`)
- The template uses `fadeVisible` binding (Magento custom binding) — not standard `visible`

