## 4. Order Repository & Management

### 4.1 OrderRepositoryInterface

**Namespace:** `Magento\Sales\Api\OrderRepositoryInterface`

The standard repository for loading, saving, and searching orders.

| Method | Signature | Returns | Description |
|---|---|---|---|
| `get` | `get(int $id)` | `OrderInterface` | Load order by entity ID (auto-increment) |
| `getList` | `getList(SearchCriteriaInterface $criteria)` | `OrderSearchResultInterface` | Search orders |
| `save` | `save(OrderInterface $entity)` | `OrderInterface` | Persist order changes |
| `delete` | `delete(OrderInterface $entity)` | `bool` | Delete an order |

**Exam focus:**
- `get($id)` uses the **entity_id** (auto-increment), **not** the increment ID (`000000001`)
- To load by increment ID, use `OrderInterface::loadByIncrementId()` or search via `getList()` with a filter

```php
<?php
declare(strict_types=1);

use Magento\Framework\Api\SearchCriteriaBuilder;
use Magento\Sales\Api\OrderRepositoryInterface;

class OrderLoadExample
{
    public function __construct(
        private readonly OrderRepositoryInterface $orderRepository,
        private readonly SearchCriteriaBuilder $searchCriteriaBuilder,
    ) {}

    /** Load order by entity_id */
    public function loadById(int $orderId): \Magento\Sales\Api\Data\OrderInterface
    {
        return $this->orderRepository->get($orderId);
    }

    /** Load order by increment ID (e.g., "000000042") */
    public function loadByIncrementId(string $incrementId): ?\Magento\Sales\Api\Data\OrderInterface
    {
        $searchCriteria = $this->searchCriteriaBuilder
            ->addFilter('increment_id', $incrementId)
            ->setPageSize(1)
            ->create();

        $results = $this->orderRepository->getList($searchCriteria);
        $items = $results->getItems();

        return !empty($items) ? reset($items) : null;
    }
}
```

