## 8. Order Status & State Management

### 8.1 State vs Status

| Concept | Description | Examples |
|---|---|---|
| **State** | System-level lifecycle stage (hardcoded in Magento) | `new`, `pending_payment`, `processing`, `complete`, `closed`, `canceled`, `holded` |
| **Status** | Store-visible label mapped to a state (customizable) | `pending`, `pending_payment`, `processing`, `complete`, `fraud` |

**Exam focus:**
- **State** is a fixed enum; **status** is a configurable label that maps to a state
- Multiple statuses can map to one state
- `closed` state = order has been fully refunded (credit memo); `complete` = fully shipped and invoiced

### 8.2 OrderManagementInterface

**Namespace:** `Magento\Sales\Api\OrderManagementInterface`

| Method | Signature | Description |
|---|---|---|
| `hold` | `hold(int $id)` | Puts order on hold (state → `holded`) |
| `unHold` | `unHold(int $id)` | Removes hold, restores previous state |
| `cancel` | `cancel(int $id)` | Cancels the order (state → `canceled`) |
| `place` | `place(OrderInterface $order)` | Places a new order (used after quote conversion) |
| `notify` | `notify(int $id)` | Re-sends the order confirmation email |
| `getCommentsList` | `getCommentsList(int $id)` | Returns OrderStatusHistorySearchResultInterface |
| `addComment` | `addComment(int $id, OrderStatusHistoryInterface $statusHistory)` | Adds a status history comment |
| `getStatus` | `getStatus(int $id)` | Returns order status string |

**Exam focus:**
- `hold()` / `unHold()` accept order **entity_id** as integer
- `cancel()` will fail (throw exception) if the order is in `complete` or `closed` state — use `$order->canCancel()` to check first
- `hold()` transitions state to `holded` regardless of current state (except `complete`, `closed`, `canceled`)

### 8.3 Direct State/Status Manipulation

```php
<?php
declare(strict_types=1);

use Magento\Sales\Api\OrderManagementInterface;
use Magento\Sales\Api\OrderRepositoryInterface;
use Magento\Sales\Model\Order;

class OrderStatusManager
{
    public function __construct(
        private readonly OrderRepositoryInterface $orderRepository,
        private readonly OrderManagementInterface $orderManagement,
    ) {}

    public function holdOrder(int $orderId): void
    {
        // Via interface (recommended)
        $this->orderManagement->hold($orderId);
    }

    public function cancelOrder(int $orderId): void
    {
        $order = $this->orderRepository->get($orderId);

        if ($order->canCancel()) {
            $this->orderManagement->cancel($orderId);
        }
    }

    public function setCustomStatus(int $orderId, string $status): void
    {
        $order = $this->orderRepository->get($orderId);

        // Directly set status (custom statuses must be configured in Admin first)
        $order->setStatus($status);
        $order->addCommentToStatusHistory(
            "Order status updated to: {$status}",
            $status
        );

        $this->orderRepository->save($order);
    }

    public function setStateAndStatus(int $orderId): void
    {
        $order = $this->orderRepository->get($orderId);

        // setState() also sets the default status for that state if second param not provided
        $order->setState(Order::STATE_PROCESSING)
              ->setStatus(Order::STATE_PROCESSING); // 'processing'

        $this->orderRepository->save($order);
    }
}
```

