## Quick-Reference Checklist

### Cart & Quote Operations
- [ ] **`CartManagementInterface::createEmptyCart()`** — creates a guest cart, returns `int` (cart ID)
- [ ] **`CartManagementInterface::createEmptyCartForCustomer(int $customerId)`** — for authenticated customers
- [ ] **`CartManagementInterface::placeOrder(int $cartId)`** — validates & converts quote to order, returns order `entity_id`
- [ ] **`CartItemRepositoryInterface::save(CartItemInterface)`** — adds/updates a line item (requires `quoteId`, `sku`, `qty`, `productType`)
- [ ] **`CartRepositoryInterface::get($id)`** — loads any quote; `getActive($id)` throws if inactive
- [ ] Always call `cartRepository->save($quote)` after modifying quote properties
- [ ] `placeOrder()` validates: shipping address, shipping method, payment method, inventory, coupon codes, totals

### Custom Total Model
- [ ] Extend **`Magento\Quote\Model\Quote\Address\Total\AbstractTotal`**
- [ ] `collect()` signature: `collect(Quote $quote, ShippingAssignmentInterface $shippingAssignment, Total $total)`
- [ ] Call `parent::collect()` **first** to reset the total
- [ ] Use `$total->addTotalAmount(code, amount)` AND `$total->addBaseTotalAmount(code, baseAmount)` to register amounts
- [ ] Also set the value on the quote object (`$quote->setData(...)`) for persistence to the order
- [ ] Guard against empty `$shippingAssignment->getItems()` to avoid double-counting
- [ ] Register in **`sales.xml`** (NOT di.xml) under `<section name="quote"><group name="totals">` with `sort_order` < 550 (`grand_total`)

### Custom Checkout Step
- [ ] Requires **both**: PHP `LayoutProcessorInterface` implementation AND JS component
- [ ] LayoutProcessor is registered via **`etc/frontend/di.xml`** on `Magento\Checkout\Block\Onepage` (NOT layout XML)
- [ ] LayoutProcessor is injected as a `layoutProcessors` constructor argument
- [ ] JS must call `stepNavigator.registerStep(code, alias, title, isVisible, navigateFn, sortOrder)`
- [ ] `isVisible` must be a **KnockoutJS observable** (`ko.observable(false)`)
- [ ] Template uses `fadeVisible` binding (Magento custom KO binding)

### Order Repository
- [ ] `OrderRepositoryInterface::get(int $id)` — loads by **entity_id** (not increment ID)
- [ ] To load by increment ID: use `getList()` with a `SearchCriteriaBuilder` filter on `increment_id`
- [ ] `getList()` returns `OrderSearchResultInterface`

### Invoice Creation
- [ ] `InvoiceService::prepareInvoice($order, $qtys)` — creates invoice object (not persisted)
- [ ] `$invoice->register()` — updates item quantities, triggers capture if `CAPTURE_ONLINE`
- [ ] `InvoiceManagementInterface::setCapture(int $invoiceId)` — triggers online payment capture for online methods (NO `pay()` method exists)
- [ ] `CAPTURE_ONLINE` vs `CAPTURE_OFFLINE` — set via `$invoice->setRequestedCaptureCase()`
- [ ] Save invoice + order atomically using `Magento\Framework\DB\Transaction`
- [ ] Check `$order->canInvoice()` before attempting

### Shipment Creation
- [ ] Use **`ShipmentFactory::create($order, $items, $tracks)`** to create the shipment object
- [ ] `$shipment->register()` — updates `qty_shipped`, transitions order state to `complete` if fully shipped
- [ ] Virtual products must be skipped — check `$orderItem->getIsVirtual()`
- [ ] Check `$order->canShip()` before attempting

### Credit Memo Creation
- [ ] `CreditmemoFactory::createByInvoice($invoice, $data)` — preferred for invoice-linked refunds
- [ ] `CreditmemoFactory::createByOrder($order, $data)` — for order-level refunds
- [ ] `CreditmemoService::refund($creditmemo, $offlineRefund)` — handles `register()` internally
- [ ] `$offlineRefund = true` → no gateway call; `false` → online gateway refund
- [ ] `adjustment_positive` = extra credit to customer; `adjustment_negative` = deduction (restocking fee)

### Order State & Status Management
- [ ] **State** is a system lifecycle stage (immutable enum); **Status** is a configurable label mapping to a state
- [ ] `OrderManagementInterface::hold(int $id)` → state = `holded`
- [ ] `OrderManagementInterface::unHold(int $id)` → restores previous state
- [ ] `OrderManagementInterface::cancel(int $id)` → state = `canceled`; fails on `complete`/`closed`
- [ ] Always check `$order->canCancel()` / `$order->canHold()` before calling management methods
- [ ] `Order::STATE_COMPLETE` = invoiced + shipped; `Order::STATE_CLOSED` = fully refunded

### Critical Tricky Points
- [ ] `placeOrder()` re-runs `collectTotals()` — custom total models **will fire again**
- [ ] Creating an invoice with `CAPTURE_ONLINE` sends a real charge to the payment gateway
- [ ] Quote is **deactivated** (not deleted) after `placeOrder()` succeeds
- [ ] `CreditmemoService::refund()` calls `register()` internally — do **not** call it manually
- [ ] For the custom checkout step: missing `LayoutProcessor` = step config never reaches JS; missing `stepNavigator.registerStep()` = step never shows in progress bar
- [ ] LayoutProcessors are registered in `etc/frontend/di.xml`, NOT in layout XML (constructor args, not `$data`)
- [ ] `CartItemRepositoryInterface::save()` for configurable products requires `productOption` with selected values

