## 1. Overview & Architecture

Magento 2 provides two primary patterns for working with entities programmatically:

| Pattern | Interface | Status | Plugin Support |
|---|---|---|---|
| Repository (Service Layer) | `RepositoryInterface` | **Recommended** | Yes — full interception |
| Direct Model save/load | `AbstractModel` | **Legacy** | Partial — bypasses some plugins |

### Entity Layer Diagram

```
+-----------------------------+
|      Service Layer          |  <-- Repositories, Service Contracts
+-----------------------------+
           |
+-----------------------------+
|      Domain Layer           |  <-- Data Models (DataObject / ExtensibleDataObject)
+-----------------------------+
           |
+-----------------------------+
|   Persistence Layer         |  <-- ResourceModel, Collection
+-----------------------------+
           |
+-----------------------------+
|       Database              |  <-- MySQL / MariaDB
+-----------------------------+
```

- **Exam focus:** The repository pattern is the **only** recommended approach in new Magento 2 development. Direct model `save()` bypasses plugin interception chains.

---

## 2. Repository Pattern (Recommended)

### 2.1 Core Concepts

Repositories implement **service contracts** defined in `Api/` interfaces. They sit between business logic and the persistence layer and are the correct extension point for CRUD operations.

```
ProductRepositoryInterface
  -> getById($id)
  -> get($sku)
  -> save($product)
  -> delete($product)
  -> deleteById($sku)
  -> getList(SearchCriteriaInterface $searchCriteria)
```

### 2.2 Loading an Entity via Repository

```php
<?php
declare(strict_types=1);

namespace Vendor\Module\Model;

use Magento\Catalog\Api\ProductRepositoryInterface;
use Magento\Framework\Exception\NoSuchEntityException;

class ProductService
{
    public function __construct(
        private readonly ProductRepositoryInterface $productRepository
    ) {}

    public function getProductBySku(string $sku): ?\Magento\Catalog\Api\Data\ProductInterface
    {
        try {
            return $this->productRepository->get($sku);
        } catch (NoSuchEntityException $e) {
            // Log or handle missing entity
            return null;
        }
    }

    public function getProductById(int $id): ?\Magento\Catalog\Api\Data\ProductInterface
    {
        try {
            return $this->productRepository->getById($id);
        } catch (NoSuchEntityException $e) {
            return null;
        }
    }
}
```

- **Exam focus:** `get()` loads by SKU; `getById()` loads by entity ID. Both are methods on `ProductRepositoryInterface`.

### 2.3 Saving an Entity via Repository

```php
<?php

use Magento\Catalog\Api\ProductRepositoryInterface;
use Magento\Catalog\Api\Data\ProductInterfaceFactory;

class ProductUpdater
{
    public function __construct(
        private readonly ProductRepositoryInterface $productRepository,
        private readonly ProductInterfaceFactory $productFactory
    ) {}

    /**
     * Create a new product using the factory + repository save.
     */
    public function createProduct(): void
    {
        $product = $this->productFactory->create();
        $product->setSku('MY-NEW-SKU-001');
        $product->setName('My New Product');
        $product->setPrice(29.99);
        $product->setAttributeSetId(4); // Default attribute set
        $product->setTypeId(\Magento\Catalog\Model\Product\Type::TYPE_SIMPLE);
        $product->setStatus(\Magento\Catalog\Model\Product\Attribute\Source\Status::STATUS_ENABLED);
        $product->setVisibility(\Magento\Catalog\Model\Product\Visibility::VISIBILITY_BOTH);

        // repository->save() triggers all before/after plugins
        $savedProduct = $this->productRepository->save($product);
    }

    /**
     * Update an existing product: load via repository, mutate, save via repository.
     */
    public function updateProductPrice(string $sku, float $newPrice): void
    {
        $product = $this->productRepository->get($sku);
        $product->setPrice($newPrice);
        $this->productRepository->save($product);
    }
}
```

- **Exam focus:** Always use `$repository->save($entity)` — **never** call `$model->save()` on an entity loaded through a repository in production code.

### 2.4 Searching with SearchCriteria

```php
<?php

use Magento\Framework\Api\SearchCriteriaBuilder;
use Magento\Framework\Api\SortOrderBuilder;
use Magento\Catalog\Api\ProductRepositoryInterface;

class ProductSearch
{
    public function __construct(
        private readonly ProductRepositoryInterface $productRepository,
        private readonly SearchCriteriaBuilder $searchCriteriaBuilder,
        private readonly SortOrderBuilder $sortOrderBuilder
    ) {}

    public function findActiveProducts(float $minPrice): array
    {
        $sortOrder = $this->sortOrderBuilder
            ->setField('price')
            ->setAscendingDirection()
            ->create();

        $searchCriteria = $this->searchCriteriaBuilder
            ->addFilter('status', 1)                // eq by default
            ->addFilter('price', $minPrice, 'gteq') // condition type as 3rd arg
            ->addSortOrder($sortOrder)
            ->setPageSize(20)
            ->setCurrentPage(1)
            ->create();

        $results = $this->productRepository->getList($searchCriteria);

        return $results->getItems(); // array of ProductInterface
    }
}
```

**SearchCriteriaBuilder filter condition types** (same set as `addFieldToFilter`):

| Condition | Meaning |
|---|---|
| `eq` | Equal (default) |
| `neq` | Not equal |
| `like` | SQL LIKE |
| `in` | IN array |
| `nin` | NOT IN array |
| `notnull` | IS NOT NULL |
| `null` | IS NULL |
| `gt` | Greater than |
| `gteq` | Greater than or equal |
| `lt` | Less than |
| `lteq` | Less than or equal |
| `from` | Range start (dates) |
| `to` | Range end (dates) |

- **Exam focus:** `addFilter($field, $value, $conditionType)` — the third argument defaults to `'eq'` if omitted.

