## 6. Pagination with Collections

### 6.1 setPageSize() and setCurPage()

```php
<?php

class PaginatedProductList
{
    public function __construct(
        private readonly \Magento\Catalog\Model\ResourceModel\Product\CollectionFactory $collectionFactory
    ) {}

    public function getPage(int $page = 1, int $pageSize = 20): array
    {
        $collection = $this->collectionFactory->create();

        $collection->addAttributeToSelect(['name', 'sku', 'price']);
        $collection->addAttributeToFilter('status', 1);

        // Pagination
        $collection->setPageSize($pageSize); // LIMIT n
        $collection->setCurPage($page);       // OFFSET (page-1)*n

        return [
            'items'        => $collection->getItems(),
            'total_count'  => $collection->getSize(),    // Total records (ignores pagination)
            'current_page' => $collection->getCurPage(),
            'page_size'    => $collection->getPageSize(),
            'last_page'    => $collection->getLastPageNumber(),
        ];
    }
}
```

### 6.2 Important Pagination Notes

```
setPageSize(20)  ->  SQL: LIMIT 20
setCurPage(3)    ->  SQL: LIMIT 20 OFFSET 40   (zero-indexed offset = (page-1) * size)

getSize()        ->  executes a separate COUNT(*) query — does NOT load items
getItems()       ->  executes the main SELECT with LIMIT/OFFSET
```

- **Exam focus:** `getSize()` fires a **separate COUNT query** — it ignores `setPageSize()` and `setCurPage()` and returns the **total matching records**. Use `getLastPageNumber()` to get total pages.

### 6.3 Adding Sort Order

```php
<?php

$collection->addAttributeToSelect('*');
$collection->setOrder('price', 'ASC');         // Standard sort
$collection->addAttributeToSort('name', 'DESC'); // Alternative method
$collection->setPageSize(10)->setCurPage(1);
```

