## 7. Mass Action / Bulk Operations

### 7.1 Using Collections for Bulk Updates

```php
<?php

use Magento\Catalog\Model\ResourceModel\Product\CollectionFactory;
use Magento\Catalog\Api\ProductRepositoryInterface;

class BulkProductDisabler
{
    public function __construct(
        private readonly CollectionFactory $collectionFactory,
        private readonly ProductRepositoryInterface $productRepository
    ) {}

    /**
     * Disable all products below a certain price threshold.
     * Uses repository->save() to maintain plugin interception.
     */
    public function disableProductsBelowPrice(float $priceThreshold): int
    {
        $collection = $this->collectionFactory->create();
        $collection->addAttributeToFilter('price', ['lt' => $priceThreshold]);
        $collection->addAttributeToFilter('status', 1); // only enabled products

        $count = 0;
        foreach ($collection as $product) {
            // Load fresh via repository to get full object with extension attributes
            $fullProduct = $this->productRepository->getById((int) $product->getId());
            $fullProduct->setStatus(\Magento\Catalog\Model\Product\Attribute\Source\Status::STATUS_DISABLED);
            $this->productRepository->save($fullProduct);
            $count++;
        }

        return $count;
    }
}
```

### 7.2 Direct Collection Update (High-Performance Bulk)

For large-scale updates where plugin interception is not needed (e.g., internal data migrations):

```php
<?php

use Magento\Framework\App\ResourceConnection;

class BulkDirectUpdater
{
    public function __construct(
        private readonly ResourceConnection $resourceConnection
    ) {}

    /**
     * Direct SQL UPDATE — bypasses all ORM, plugins, events.
     * Use only for migrations or when performance is critical
     * and you are certain no plugins must run.
     */
    public function bulkSetSpecialPrice(array $productIds, float $specialPrice): void
    {
        $connection = $this->resourceConnection->getConnection();
        $tableName  = $this->resourceConnection->getTableName('catalog_product_entity_decimal');

        // Get attribute ID for special_price
        $attributeId = $connection->fetchOne(
            "SELECT attribute_id FROM {$this->resourceConnection->getTableName('eav_attribute')}
             WHERE attribute_code = 'special_price'
               AND entity_type_id = 4"
        );

        $connection->update(
            $tableName,
            ['value' => $specialPrice],
            [
                'attribute_id = ?' => $attributeId,
                'entity_id IN (?)' => $productIds,
            ]
        );
    }
}
```

- **Exam focus:** Direct SQL updates via `ResourceConnection` completely bypass EAV value management, cache invalidation, index updates, and all event/plugin systems. Only use for raw migrations.

### 7.3 Asynchronous Bulk Operations (Bulk API)

```php
<?php
// Magento ships with BulkManagementInterface for async operations
use Magento\AsynchronousOperations\Api\BulkStatusInterface;
use Magento\Framework\Bulk\BulkManagementInterface;
use Magento\Framework\DataObject\IdentityGeneratorInterface;

// Bulk operations use Message Queue (RabbitMQ or MySQL queue)
// Operations are dispatched and processed asynchronously
// Each operation is a serialized payload processed by a consumer
```

