## 8. DB Transaction Handling

### 8.1 ResourceConnection Transaction API

```php
<?php

use Magento\Framework\App\ResourceConnection;

class TransactionalUpdater
{
    public function __construct(
        private readonly ResourceConnection $resourceConnection
    ) {}

    public function updateMultipleRecordsAtomically(array $updates): void
    {
        $connection = $this->resourceConnection->getConnection();

        // Begin transaction — wraps all subsequent queries in a transaction
        $connection->beginTransaction();

        try {
            foreach ($updates as $update) {
                $connection->update(
                    $this->resourceConnection->getTableName($update['table']),
                    $update['data'],
                    $update['where']
                );
            }

            // All operations succeeded — commit
            $connection->commit();

        } catch (\Exception $e) {
            // Any failure — rollback ALL changes
            $connection->rollBack();

            // Re-throw so the caller knows the operation failed
            throw $e;
        }
    }
}
```

### 8.2 Nested Transactions with Savepoints

```php
<?php

$connection->beginTransaction(); // Outer transaction

try {
    $connection->insert($table1, $data1);

    // Magento's adapter handles nested beginTransaction() via savepoints
    $connection->beginTransaction(); // Creates a SAVEPOINT internally
    try {
        $connection->insert($table2, $data2);
        $connection->commit(); // Releases savepoint
    } catch (\Exception $e) {
        $connection->rollBack(); // Rolls back to savepoint only
        // Outer transaction is still active
    }

    $connection->commit(); // Commits outer transaction
} catch (\Exception $e) {
    $connection->rollBack(); // Rolls back everything
}
```

### 8.3 Transaction with Repository Operations

```php
<?php

use Magento\Framework\App\ResourceConnection;
use Magento\Catalog\Api\ProductRepositoryInterface;

class TransactionalRepositoryService
{
    public function __construct(
        private readonly ResourceConnection $resourceConnection,
        private readonly ProductRepositoryInterface $productRepository
    ) {}

    /**
     * NOTE: Repository operations call their own save() which may use
     * the same connection. Wrapping them in a connection-level transaction
     * does NOT fully capture all repository-level side effects
     * (like cache invalidation). Use with care.
     */
    public function atomicProductUpdates(array $skus, float $newPrice): void
    {
        $connection = $this->resourceConnection->getConnection();
        $connection->beginTransaction();

        try {
            foreach ($skus as $sku) {
                $product = $this->productRepository->get($sku);
                $product->setPrice($newPrice);
                $this->productRepository->save($product);
            }

            $connection->commit();
        } catch (\Exception $e) {
            $connection->rollBack();
            throw $e;
        }
    }
}
```

- **Exam focus:** `beginTransaction()`, `commit()`, and `rollBack()` are methods on the **connection object** returned by `ResourceConnection::getConnection()`, not on `ResourceConnection` itself.

