## 11. Tricky Exam Gotchas

### 11.1 The save() Anti-Pattern

```php
<?php
// WRONG — bypasses repository plugins
$product = $productRepository->getById(1);
$product->setPrice(99.99);
$product->save(); // <-- NEVER DO THIS

// CORRECT — goes through full service layer
$product = $productRepository->getById(1);
$product->setPrice(99.99);
$productRepository->save($product); // <-- CORRECT
```

### 11.2 Plain Array Creates OR, NOT IN

```php
<?php
// WRONG assumption — plain array does NOT create IN:
$collection->addFieldToFilter('entity_id', [1, 2, 3]);
// Actually produces: (entity_id = 1) OR (entity_id = 2) OR (entity_id = 3)

// CORRECT way to create IN condition:
$collection->addFieldToFilter('entity_id', ['in' => [1, 2, 3]]);
// Produces: entity_id IN (1, 2, 3)

// Scalar value uses eq condition:
$collection->addFieldToFilter('entity_id', 1);
// Equivalent to:
$collection->addFieldToFilter('entity_id', ['eq' => 1]);
```

### 11.3 ResourceModel _construct() vs __construct()

```php
<?php
class Article extends AbstractDb
{
    // This is the AbstractDb initialization hook — NOT the PHP constructor
    // Called by AbstractDb's __construct() automatically
    protected function _construct(): void
    {
        $this->_init('table_name', 'primary_key');
    }

    // PHP constructor — for DI injection
    public function __construct(
        \Magento\Framework\Model\ResourceModel\Db\Context $context,
        // ... other dependencies
        $connectionName = null
    ) {
        parent::__construct($context, $connectionName);
        // _construct() is called by parent::__construct()
    }
}
```

### 11.4 getSize() vs count($collection->getItems())

```php
<?php
$collection->setPageSize(10)->setCurPage(2);

$collection->getSize();           // Returns TOTAL matching records (e.g., 150)
                                  // Runs COUNT(*) without LIMIT

count($collection->getItems());   // Returns count of LOADED items (e.g., 10)
                                  // Limited by setPageSize()
```

### 11.5 addFieldToFilter vs addAttributeToFilter

```
Flat table column  ->  addFieldToFilter()
EAV attribute      ->  addAttributeToFilter()

Product Collections:   addAttributeToFilter() (products use EAV)
Order Collections:     addFieldToFilter() (orders use flat tables)
```

### 11.6 Area Code in Data Patches

```php
<?php
// Data patches execute in CLI context (no area code set by default)
// Loading products that use area-dependent logic (layout, design) will fail
// without explicitly setting an area code:

$this->appState->emulateAreaCode(
    \Magento\Framework\App\Area::AREA_ADMINHTML,
    function () {
        // Code here runs with adminhtml area
        $this->productRepository->get('some-sku');
    }
);

// Without this, you may get:
// Magento\Framework\Exception\LocalizedException: Area code not set
```

### 11.7 CollectionProcessor — Automatic SearchCriteria Application

```php
<?php
// CollectionProcessorInterface resolves:
// - SearchCriteria filters   -> addFieldToFilter() calls
// - SearchCriteria sortOrders -> setOrder() calls
// - SearchCriteria page size  -> setPageSize() / setCurPage() calls

// Without CollectionProcessor, you'd have to manually translate
// SearchCriteria to Collection method calls — CollectionProcessor does it for you.

// Inject: Magento\Framework\Api\SearchCriteria\CollectionProcessorInterface
// Default implementation: Magento\Framework\Api\SearchCriteria\CollectionProcessor
```

### 11.8 Transaction Rollback Does Not Undo Cache

```
Transaction rollback:    Undoes database writes within the transaction
Does NOT undo:           - Cache entries written during the transaction
                         - External service calls
                         - Message queue publishes
                         - File system changes

Always handle non-DB side effects manually when rolling back.
```

